Subject: symtrz.f: restore NADIM in the ten short COMMON /S00002/ declarations

WHAT IT FIXES
  A second real MOPAC 7.00 defect, also fixed in MOPAC 7.01.

  symtrz.f shares /S00002/ from thirteen subprograms. Three of them declare
  seven members:

      COMMON /S00002/ NUMAT,NORBS,NADIM,NCDIM,IQUAL,NDORBS,IERROR

  and ten declare six, with NADIM missing:

      COMMON /S00002/ NUMAT,NORBS,NCDIM,IQUAL,NDORBS,IERROR

  Every member after the second is therefore off by one slot in those ten:
  what they call NCDIM is really NADIM, what they call IERROR is really
  NDORBS, and IERROR itself is read from past the block. f2c says so, if you
  do not pass -w:

      Warning on line 179 of symtrz.f: incompatible lengths
                                       for common block s00002
      ... and nine more

  The visible symptom is that MOPAC fails to recognise the molecular point
  group -- ethene, benzene and pyridine all print

      MOLECULAR POINT GROUP   :   ????

  and every orbital's symmetry label comes out as `0 ????`, which is the one
  thing MOPAC 7 is used for here. With the declaration restored they print
  D2H, D6H and C2V, and the labels come out (1AG, 1B1U, ...).

  MOPAC 7.01 carries the seven-member form in all thirteen places; this patch
  makes 7.00 match it.

--- a/symtrz.f
+++ b/symtrz.f
@@ -167,7 +167,7 @@
       INCLUDE 'SIZES'
       PARAMETER (MXDIM=MAXPAR+NUMATM)
       CHARACTER*4 NAME,NAMO,ISTA
-      COMMON /S00002/ NUMAT,NORBS,NCDIM,IQUAL,NDORBS,IERROR
+      COMMON /S00002/ NUMAT,NORBS,NADIM,NCDIM,IQUAL,NDORBS,IERROR
       COMMON /S00003/ IELEM(20),ELEM(3,3,20),CUB(3,3),JELEM(20,NUMATM)
       COMMON /S00004/ SHIFT(3),R(3,3),VECT(2,MXDIM)
       COMMON/SYMRES/ TRANS,RTR,SIG,NAME,NAMO(MXDIM),INDEX(MXDIM),ISTA(2)
@@ -334,7 +334,7 @@
       IMPLICIT DOUBLE PRECISION (A-H,O-Z)
